<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="36d7c2af">&lt;p&gt;
    There&amp;nbsp;are a multitude of Agile project management tools available in the market that should be considered to
    better enable teams in the management and execution of their work. When assessing such tools remember to consider some
    of the below capabilities during the decision making process.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Progress visualization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
        Tools can make it easy to see the progress of each team member with respect to their assigned projects or tasks.
        The tool may also offer the capability to generate a visual view of such progress (i.e. Scrum Board) in order to
        make it easier to identify obstacles and track issues requiring immediate attention.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Estimation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
        Tools can also assist in controlling scope creep and with setting accurate requirements in order to calculate how
        long a sprint will take. Accurate time estimations can then be used to generate historical data that can be used in
        forecasting future projects.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Project portfolio management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
        Tools may offer the ability to scale and avoid being cumbersome when responding to change. Having access to an
        entire portfolio of projects makes managing multiple Scrum teams within a project, as well as multiple separate
        projects, easier.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Risk management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
        Tools with the ability to calculate risks in advance have the ability to limit unexpected expenditures, delays and
        quality deterioration. This becomes increasingly valuable for long-term and complicated projects where unforeseen
        circumstances are more likely.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Resource management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
        Tools with resource management features allow teams to improve their resource planning. Being able to see who is
        over or under assigned work in real-time&amp;nbsp;allows for quicker reassignment of work to maintain both efficiencies
        as well as a healthy balance between time allocated for innovation versus work.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Scrum events&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
        Tools may also offer the ability to catalog findings, comments, actions or changes recorded as part of various
        Scrum ceremonies (e.g. sprint planning, sprint review, sprint retrospective). This information can then be easily
        tracked and leveraged as needed.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Selecting the right tool will depend upon both the necessary capabilities required to meet the client&apos;s needs as well
    as factors such as:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Maturity of Agile methodology in the client organization
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Current Agile delivery framework being used by the client (Scrum, Kanban, XP, etc.)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Size of the client&apos;s project portfolio and the expected number of users for the tool
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Types of roles expected to use the tool (Product Owners, Managers, IT PMs, etc.)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Degree to which the client&apos;s portfolio strategy is linked to EY&apos;s Agile execution strategy
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Extent of tool configurations required by the client
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Importance of tool integration with other applications
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Client&apos;s available budget for such a tool
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Some of the more common tools include:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Agile Central (Rally)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Version One
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        JIRA
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        IBM Rational Team Concert (RTC)
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    For detailed comparisons on the above mentioned four tools please refer to the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;elementLink&quot;
    href=&quot;./../../../practice.mgmt.proj.agile_pm.base/guidances/supportingmaterials/agile_tools_mrkt_insight_E85BE62E.html&quot;
    guid=&quot;_sDi_4ESiEeiASMlqgAcI7A&quot;&gt;Agile Tools Market Insights&lt;/a&gt;.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
